# SBFB Sprint 77 Phase F1 — pipeline layer-split fork of llama.cpp
# Base: llama-cpp-sys-2 0.1.146 bundled llama.cpp (utilityai/llama-cpp-rs sha 4afdaf0).
# Backend-agnostic (CUDA/Metal/CPU): partial-decode API (proven bit-exact at spike)
# + TENSOR_SKIP partial load (P-D, S77 F1). Apply with: patch -p1 < this file, from
# vendor/llama-cpp-sys-2/llama.cpp/. Rust-side setters/batch live in vendor/llama-cpp-2/.
#
# SBFB Sprint 77 Phase F2 — Rust-side addition (committed directly in
# vendor/llama-cpp-2/src/gguf/mod.rs, same convention as the F1 setters/batch):
# GgufContext gains tensor_name / tensor_size / tensor_type accessors over the
# already-bound FFI (gguf_get_tensor_name/size/type), plus typed metadata getters
# meta_str / meta_u32 (type-checked find_key + val_*; they keep the GGUF_TYPE_*
# discriminants inside this crate so worker-core needs no llama-cpp-sys-2 dep).
# Used by the worker shard claim gate to estimate per-shard VRAM from the GGUF
# header (block-quant-aware sizes computed by ggml itself, no hand-rolled
# type-size table). No C++ change.
#
